{"id":134661006159939,"type":"album","name":"Loaded","artist":"The Velvet Underground","year":1970,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710708.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-3645588f-cdcf-4746-97ac-da059d332010/mbid-3645588f-cdcf-4746-97ac-da059d332010-4529718708.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":14,"country":"US","aoty":100,"aoty_user":81,"yt":"AqVWBVbytXo","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-velvet-underground/loaded","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/5738-the-velvet-underground-loaded.php"},"desc":"Loaded is the fourth album by The Velvet Underground, released in November 1970, by Atlantic Records' subsidiary label, Cotillion. The album was the final album recorded featuring Lou Reed, though he had departed from the band shortly before the album's release. In 2003, Loaded was #109 on Rolling Stone's reissue of their 500 greatest albums of all time. Loaded was a commercial effort aimed at radio play, another step away from the Warhol-influenced days. The album's title refers to Atlantic's request that the band produce an album \"loaded with hits\". Doug Yule said, \"On Loaded there was a big push ."},"artist_ref":{"id":132878248289584,"name":"The Velvet Underground","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Velvet_Underground_1968_by_Billy_Name.png?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":621,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":207419651019004,"type":"genre","name":"Garage Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":556,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":55893123468232,"type":"genre","name":"Experimental Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":373,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id"